WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.010
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:07.290
Names like Hitler, Stalin and Mao Zedong are
often thrown around as some of the evilest

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.679
men to have walked the Earth; each one causing
the deaths of many millions.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:18.920
But there’s a man equally as a despicable
as Adolf Hitler, yet very few people even

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.070
known of his existence.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:27.599
King Leopold II is one of the least reviled
tyrants from history, yet he was directly

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:33.620
responsible for the deaths of an estimated
15 million people, he caused a hidden holocaust

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:40.500
that is rarely mentioned, devastating an entire
country, murdering the vast majority of its

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.500
population.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.960
So why is so little spoken about King Leopold
II?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.780
Some say it’s because he only murdered Africans.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.390
Leopold was the King of the Belgians between
1865 and 1909.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:59.820
Nothing about his upbringing spelled “genocidal
psychopath”; as a young prince he was perfectly

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.280
well behaved, an upstanding member of the
royal family.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:10.090
But it all went to pot when gained ownership
of The Congo in 1885.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:15.910
But let’s just rewind a little, how does
a Kind in Belgium come to own a large country

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.740
smack bang in the middle of Africa?

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:24.290
Throughout the late 1800s Africa was being
slammed by Europe, multiple European countries

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:29.090
attempted to and successfully colonized vast
parts of the continent.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.590
The methodology behind all this colonization
was basically…

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:37.409
oh look, Africa isn’t as civilized or technologically
advanced as us – let’s take their land

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:42.500
and freedom then force them to practice our
religion, use our technology and we’ll take

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.650
all the profits from their mineral rich land
– surely that’s a better life than what

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.560
they’re use to, no?

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.480
The British empire came first and claimed
the South, the North East and bits of the

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.480
North West.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.380
The French took the North East and Madagascar,
the rest was snatched up by the Italians and

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.899
Portuguese, oh and Germany got their hans
on a few bits as well.

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:09.100
This left one massive gaping hole in the center
of Africa.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.580
The Congo was the hardest to take because
it was far from the coast and was covered

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.660
in treacherous jungle.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.640
Leopold set his eyes on it, knowing it was
rich in natural resources such as rubber,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.360
which was highly valuable in those days.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.910
So how exactly did Leopold come to own the
Congo?

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:35.050
Bearing in mind it is 76 times the size of
Belgium and was home to millions of people.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.520
Did he simply invade and stick flags everywhere?

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:44.250
Nope, he basically said to the world’s most
powerful nations “Hey if you guys aren’t

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.810
using this bit, can I have it?”

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:50.100
and they said “sure, if you give us a bit
of money for it”.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.940
However, the Congo was different to other
African states.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:58.030
Unlike the others, such as South Africa and
the Spanish Sahara, which were colonies of

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:04.780
European governments, the Congo Free State
as it was known, was deemed the private property

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.260
of one man – his own personal play thing.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:16.580
Leopold formed the International African Society,
which was a supposedly philanthropic scheme

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:21.290
to “help” Africans by introducing them
to Christianity and giving them clothes.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:27.340
But this was just a ruse to get the Belgian
government to give him money to startup his

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.340
supposed “humanitarian” project in Africa.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:38.400
What Leopold actually did in the Congo was
far from “humanitarian” – he forced

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:45.310
the Congolese people into hard labour, so
hard that millions died from exhaustion, disease

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:47.290
and starvation.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.850
The unfortunate natives were forced to dig
up gold, hunt and kill elephants for their

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:57.560
ivory and chop down hundreds of miles of forest,
to set up rubber plantations all across the

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.560
Congo.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.930
Gold, ivory and rubber were three of the most
expensive commodities in the world at that

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:09.980
time and King Leopold sold all the resources
he ruthlessly mined through slave-labour,

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:17.250
to European countries, in order to generate
vast, vast sums of money for his own personal

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.250
enjoyment.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:24.820
As if all that wasn’t enough, Leopold also
sold swathes of Congolese into slavery.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.630
So how did King Leopold organize such a large
operation across an enormous country with

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.150
millions of natives.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:39.270
He was very smart and basically used his wealth
and power to turn the Congolese people against

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.620
themselves.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:45.620
He recruited a large army of mercenaries which
he named the “Force Publique” made up

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:52.580
of Congolese natives and paid them to enforce
his ruthless regime against their own people.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:58.220
Leopold setup a hierarchy, handpicking the
most loyal members of the Force Publique to

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:02.170
become governors over a specific region of
the country.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:07.610
Governors would be given complete dictatorial
control over their realm and they had quotas

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:11.720
of ivory, gold and rubber that they had to
enforce.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:17.940
If workers didn’t meet their monthly quota
of raw materials, they were mutilated.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:21.640
The most common way was to amputate their
hands and feet.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:29.120
And if they fled town, the Force Publique
would amputate the limbs of their entire family.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.090
Governors were paid by commission, so it was
in their interest to force those under their

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:37.180
control to work even harder.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.890
The result of this is that millions of natives
were literally worked to death either down

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.950
the mines or in the fields.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:50.610
If you don’t already hate this guy enough,
he also used the Congo as a giant hunting

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:55.480
ground for himself and his wealthy friends
– where they freely hunted animals such

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.420
as lions and elephants.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:03.570
No one knows for sure what the exact population
of the Congo was before it was colonized by

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:07.080
King Leopold, since it was so remote and dangerous.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.570
But it’s estimated it was over 20 million.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:19.300
By the end of King Leopold’s reign of terror,
the population had dropped to well under 10

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.300
million.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.930
So what ended his tyranny?

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:23.930
Competition.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:30.280
(1) The United States, Britain and the Netherlands
owned large rubber-producing colonies of their

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:36.330
own and so King Leopold’s efforts were stifling
their profits on the global market.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:42.530
The three nations forced Leopold to surrender
his land and hand it back to the Belgian Government.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:47.400
Whom by the way still treated the Congolese
people horrifically for many years afterwards

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:53.920
– it wasn’t until the country gained independence
in 1971 that the Congo was free from the tyranny

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:59.480
of Belgium, but the ripples of history run
deep throughout the land - they still have

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.980
a long way to go to achieve political stability
today.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.340
Thanks for watching.

